+### Directory Not Empty
+
+If you see an error like this:
+
+```bash
+npm ERR! code ENOTEMPTY
+npm ERR! syscall rename
+npm ERR! path /Users/my-user/.nvm/versions/node/v18.18.2/lib/node_modules/codebuff
+npm ERR! dest /Users/my-user/.nvm/versions/node/v18.18.2/lib/node_modules/.codebuff-NmQAW018
+npm ERR! errno -66
+npm ERR! ENOTEMPTY: directory not empty, rename '/Users/my-user/.nvm/versions/node/v18.18.2/lib/node_modules/codebuff' -> '/Users/my-user/.nvm/versions/node/v18.18.2/lib/node_modules/.codebuff-NmQAW018'
+```
+
+It means you have a directory named `.codebuff-NmQAW018` in your node_modules directory. This is a temporary directory created by npm when installing packages. You can safely delete this directory and try again:
+
+```bash
+rm -rf /Users/my-user/.nvm/versions/node/v18.18.2/lib/node_modules/.codebuff-NmQAW018
+```
+
